<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt-based Baseline Prompts</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Prompt-based Baseline Prompts ‣ Appendix A Experimental Setup - Additional Details ‣ Detecting (Un)answerability in Large Language Modelswith Linear Directions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the prompt used in the standard prompt-based baseline, which contains only the context and question. Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Prompt-based Baseline Prompts ‣ Appendix A Experimental Setup - Additional Details ‣ Detecting (Un)answerability in Large Language Modelswith Linear Directions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> presents the modified version used in the abstention-instruction baseline, which encourages the model to abstain when the question cannot be answered from the passage.</p>
</div>
