<td id="A6.T17.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:2.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:28.5pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.T17.2.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SQuAD</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T17.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:2.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:48.4pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Unanswerable</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T17.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:2.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">…MCA agent Lew Wasserman made a deal with Universal for his client James Stewart…</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T17.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:2.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_p">Who was a MAC agent?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T17.2.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:2.5pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.6.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A6.T17.2.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_p">The question refers to “MAC” while the passage only mentions “MCA” so the correct label is unanswerable. However, the model may have treated this as a minor typo, leading the direction to misclassify it as answerable.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T17.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T17.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding:2.5pt 4.0pt;">
